From 2285aa5bd94e22a50bf8aa8f77557706541cd438 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mt7902-patches <patches@local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:16:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] mwx: skip MCU_UNI_CMD_SNIFFER on MT7902 init, fail fast
 on error

Root cause of the "no networks visible" stage: three runs of descriptor
forensics show the MCU TX ring frozen at index 39 - the descriptor holding
MCU_UNI_CMD_SNIFFER (0x20024) with the MT7921-style 12-byte payload.  DMA
poll reads txmcu cpu=45 dma=40 / cpu=43 dma=40: the WM firmware takes
everything up to and including mt7921_mcu_uni_add_dev (idx 37) and the
fire-and-forget 0x4001d (idx 38), swallows 0x20024 (idx 39) and never
fetches again - MCU_CE_CMD_START_HW_SCAN (0x40003, 1186 bytes) sits at
idx 40 behind the wedge and times out 3 s later, mwx_reset() hard-reloads
the firmware, init retries, wedge repeats: infinite enable/disable loop.

The MT7902 WM is connac3-generation firmware (build 20251212*, chip=0x13);
Linux mt76 only sends MCU_UNI_CMD_SNIFFER from monitor-mode channel-ctx
assignment (mt7925_assign_vif_chanctx), never from __mt7925_start().
AirportMtkWlan's HAL inherited OpenBSD mwx(4)'s MT7921-era init sequence,
which disables sniffer mode unconditionally in mwx_init().

So: skip the call on MT7902 (STA path), and check the return value of
mt7921_mcu_set_sniffer() on the other chips so a wedged MCU fails init
fast instead of starting a scan that cannot work.

Expected result: init completes, the first hw scan (0x40003) goes through
and scan results appear.

Tested on: ASUS Vivobook, MT7902 14c3:7902 / AzureWave 1a3b:5520
---
 SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp b/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp
index 9fcace7..8e63104 100644
--- a/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp
+++ b/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp
@@ -1129,9 +1129,28 @@ mwx_init_hw(struct ifnet *ifp)
 		MWX_DEV_LOG(sc, "init monitor beacon filter disable returned %d\n", rv);
 		sc->sc_rxfilter = 0;
 		mwx_set(sc, MT_DMA_DCR0(0), MT_DMA_DCR0_RXD_G5_EN);
+	} else if (sc->sc_hwtype == MWX_HW_MT7902) {
+		/*
+		 * MT7902 (connac3-generation WM firmware) wedges its MCU TX queue
+		 * when init sends MCU_UNI_CMD_SNIFFER (0x20024) with the MT7921-
+		 * style 12-byte payload: the WM stops fetching descriptors behind
+		 * it and every later command, incl. the first hw scan, times out.
+		 * Linux mt76 never sends sniffer mode outside monitor mode (see
+		 * __mt7925_start() vs mt7925_assign_vif_chanctx()), so skip it
+		 * here as well.
+		 */
+		MWX_DEV_LOG(sc, "init sniffer disable skipped on MT7902\n");
+		sc->sc_rxfilter |= MT_WF_RFCR_DROP_OTHER_UC;
+		mwx_clear(sc, MT_DMA_DCR0(0), MT_DMA_DCR0_RXD_G5_EN);
 	} else {
 		rv = mt7921_mcu_set_sniffer(sc, 0);
-		MWX_DEV_LOG(sc, "init sniffer disable returned %d\n", rv);
+		if (rv != 0) {
+			/* fail fast: do not keep init going with a wedged MCU */
+			MWX_DEV_LOG(sc, "init sniffer disable failed error=%d\n",
+			    rv);
+			return rv;
+		}
+		MWX_DEV_LOG(sc, "init sniffer disable ok\n");
 		sc->sc_rxfilter |= MT_WF_RFCR_DROP_OTHER_UC;
 		mwx_clear(sc, MT_DMA_DCR0(0), MT_DMA_DCR0_RXD_G5_EN);
 	}
